<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Files">Files</span></h3>
<p>List of the of files loaded via asset manager.
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:Error mw:File"><a href=
=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/index.php?title=3DSpecial:Upload&amp;=
wpDestFile=3DQuestionThemes8Files.png" class=3D"new" title=3D"File:Question=
Themes8Files.png"><span class=3D"mw-file-element mw-broken-media">File:Ques=
tionThemes8Files.png</span></a></span>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"General_attributes">General attribute=
s</span></h3>
<p>General attributes are attributes that are displayed on the right side o=
f the question editor.
</p><p>These attributes are predefined and are the same for all Question Th=
emes. Currently, no new ones can be added. If you want to show or hide cert=
ain options for a Question Theme, you can remove or add the attribute.
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:Error mw:File"><a href=
=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/index.php?title=3DSpecial:Upload&amp;=
wpDestFile=3DQuestionThemes9GeneralAttributes.png" class=3D"new" title=3D"F=
ile:QuestionThemes9GeneralAttributes.png"><span class=3D"mw-file-element mw=
-broken-media">File:QuestionThemes9GeneralAttributes.png</span></a></span>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Attributes">Attributes</span></h3>
<p>Attributes are options you want to give to a Question Theme and can be c=
ustomized. They are visible at the bottom of the question editor.
</p><p><span class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:Error mw:File"><a href=
=3D"https://www.limesurvey.org/manual/index.php?title=3DSpecial:Upload&amp;=
wpDestFile=3DQuestionThemes10Attributes.png" class=3D"new" title=3D"File:Qu=
estionThemes10Attributes.png"><span class=3D"mw-file-element mw-broken-medi=
a">File:QuestionThemes10Attributes.png</span></a></span>
</p>
<table class=3D"wikitable">
<tbody><tr>
<th>Tag
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>name</td>
<td>The internal name
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>category</td>
<td>The category tab in which the attribute should be displayed. This can a=
lso be a new one.
</td></tr>
<tr>
